# Engine objects that reference a symbol only a shell object defines.
#
# THREE, and all three are the same thing: engine code printing. They became
# visible when misc.h's console half moved to shell/console.h -- before that
# sync_cout and dbg_print lived in a PLATFORM file, so an engine file calling
# them produced an engine-to-platform edge and the shell check could not see it.
# The misplacement was hiding the violation, which is the argument for zoning by
# meaning rather than by where a helper happens to sit.
#
#   search.o  -> dbg_print       the periodic debug-counter dump
#   search.o  -> operator<<(SyncCout)  the Syzygy PV-extension warning
#   network.o -> operator<<(SyncCout)  the net export/save messages
#
# These are what B7 calls the OUTPUT SINK seam, and it is not built: the engine
# should declare a sink and the composition root register one, so that an
# engine driven without a UCI layer still has somewhere to say things.
network.o _ZN9StockfishlsERSoNS_8SyncCoutE
search.o _ZN9Stockfish9dbg_printEv
search.o _ZN9StockfishlsERSoNS_8SyncCoutE
